1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,453
A storybook creaks open, and a golden mirror begins to glow.

2
00:00:04,753 --> 00:00:07,953
What happens in Snow White, in the Grimms' own words?

3
00:00:08,253 --> 00:00:11,944
We follow their final edition, from eighteen fifty-seven.

4
00:00:12,244 --> 00:00:16,425
A queen wishes for a child as white as snow, as red as blood.

5
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,581
At the birth, the queen dies.

6
00:00:18,881 --> 00:00:22,316
The king remarries a proud woman with a magic mirror.

7
00:00:22,616 --> 00:00:27,501
In the first edition, from eighteen twelve, the villain was Snow White's own mother.

8
00:00:27,801 --> 00:00:29,487
Watch what else changes.

9
00:00:30,487 --> 00:00:34,327
When Snow White is seven, the mirror names her fairer than the queen.

10
00:00:34,627 --> 00:00:40,302
The queen orders a huntsman to kill the girl in the woods and bring back her lungs and liver.

11
00:00:40,602 --> 00:00:42,628
She begs, and he lets her run.

12
00:00:42,928 --> 00:00:48,539
He brings back a young boar's instead, and the queen eats them, believing they are the girl's.

13
00:00:48,839 --> 00:00:51,719
Snow White runs through thorns to a little house.

14
00:00:52,019 --> 00:00:55,966
Its seven dwarfs let her stay, but warn her: let no one in.

15
00:00:56,966 --> 00:00:59,953
The queen comes back, three times, in disguise.

16
00:01:00,253 --> 00:01:05,714
First, an old peddler woman laces her bodice so tight she falls as if dead.

17
00:01:06,014 --> 00:01:08,979
The dwarfs cut the laces, and she breathes again.

18
00:01:09,279 --> 00:01:12,565
Next, another old woman brings a poisoned comb.

19
00:01:12,865 --> 00:01:14,998
The dwarfs pull it out, and she wakes.

20
00:01:15,298 --> 00:01:20,354
Last, a peasant woman offers an apple, poisoned only on its red half.

21
00:01:20,654 --> 00:01:22,233
The queen eats the white.

22
00:01:22,533 --> 00:01:25,178
Snow White bites the red, and falls dead.

23
00:01:25,478 --> 00:01:27,099
The dwarfs cannot wake her.

24
00:01:28,099 --> 00:01:31,832
She looks so alive that the dwarfs lay her in a glass coffin.

25
00:01:32,132 --> 00:01:37,338
A prince's servants carry it away, stumble, and the apple piece shakes from her throat.

26
00:01:37,638 --> 00:01:39,088
She sits up, alive.

27
00:01:39,388 --> 00:01:45,319
At the wedding, her stepmother is made to dance in red-hot iron shoes until she falls dead.

28
00:01:45,619 --> 00:01:51,955
Disney's film dropped the first two disguised visits, named the dwarfs, and woke her with a kiss.

29
00:01:52,255 --> 00:01:53,876
The Grimms wrote a stumble.

30
00:01:54,176 --> 00:01:55,414
The book closes.

31
00:01:55,714 --> 00:01:57,143
The mirror goes dark.
